  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Promoting solar self-consumption for sustainable energy in Djibouti. Djibouti, a small country in the Horn of Africa, faces significant challenges in ensuring reliable access to electricity for its growing population and economy. By the end of 2022, approximately 60-80% of Djiboutis annual electricity consumption relied on power generated in Ethiopia, highlighting its heavy dependence on external sources. The countrys power infrastructure, managed by Electricit&#xe9; de Djibouti (EDD), is inadequate, suffering from ageing equipment, poor maintenance, and limited coverage, leaving it vulnerable to price fluctuations in global fuel markets and disruptions in the supply chain due to political tensions and climate-related events</narrative>
  </description>
